# expect: ex:reUtf8 bddo:CustomEncodingCharsetShape sh:NotConstraintComponent sh:Warning
# expect: ex:reLatin1 bddo:CustomEncodingCharsetShape sh:NotConstraintComponent sh:Warning
# expect: ex:utf16 bddo:CustomEncodingCharsetShape sh:NotConstraintComponent sh:Warning
# expect: ex:ucs2 bddo:CustomEncodingCharsetShape sh:NotConstraintComponent sh:Warning
# Custom encodings a profile should not have minted. Each is still a valid description (no
# Violation): the charset is one a processor may know. The author is advised, at sh:Warning,
# that the first two re-spell a registered encoding (names are compared ignoring case) and that
# the last two name 16-bit code units without saying which byte comes first.
@prefix bddo: <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#> .
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/enc#> .

ex:reUtf8 a bddo:CustomEncoding ; bddo:ianaCharset "utf-8" .
ex:reLatin1 a bddo:CustomEncoding ; bddo:ianaCharset "ISO-8859-1" .
ex:utf16 a bddo:CustomEncoding ; bddo:ianaCharset "UTF-16" .
ex:ucs2 a bddo:CustomEncoding ; bddo:ianaCharset "ISO-10646-UCS-2" .

# A byte-ordered charset this vocabulary does not register draws no advice.
ex:utf16leBom a bddo:CustomEncoding ; bddo:ianaCharset "x-UTF-16LE-BOM" .
